1. LITERATURE AUDIT (2000–2026)

Notation: x = ln N, F_α = x^α (ln x)^{1−α}, L_N[α, c] = exp((c + o(1)) F_α). Labels: [PROVED], [MODEL-PROVED], [HEURISTIC], [MODEL-ASSUMPTION].

A. Zhu, Lv, and Liu (2025 online / Feb 2026 print), "On the complexity formulae of the number field sieve and its variants", Designs, Codes and Cryptography 94:51 (doi 10.1007/s10623-025-01788-5; noted in [nfsfruit_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/nfsfruit_results.md#L152-L154)).
- What they prove and in what model: Working inside the standard heuristic NFS/TNFS/MNFS/exTNFS parameter space for discrete logarithms in F_Q (Q = p^n) and factoring (Q = N), they replace ad hoc Lagrange-multiplier optimizations (e.g. Kim–Barbulescu 2016 Table 4, Barbulescu–Pierrot 2014) with elementary closed-form expressions for c in L_Q[1/3, c] as functions of polynomial degrees, coefficient heights, sieving dimension t ≥ 2, and field count V = L_Q[1/3, v], assuming full-box sieving E^t, Dickman smoothness on typical coefficient-height norms, and quadratic sparse linear algebra (ω = 2). Within these formulae, they prove every variant satisfies c ≥ (32/9)^{1/3} ≈ 1.5263 (the SNFS/SexTNFS floor).
- Mechanism and limits: For one pair (v = 0) with scaled degrees d_i = δ_i (x/ln x)^{1/3} and log-heights η_i F_{2/3}, Q | Res(f_0, f_1) forces δ_1 η_0 + δ_0 η_1 ≥ 1, minimizing c at (32/9)^{1/3} (t = 2, δ_0 = 0, η_1 = 0). Crucially, for MNFS (V ≥ 2 sides sharing a root mod Q), pairwise resultant divisibility Q | Res(f_{1,i}, f_{1,j}) forces 2 δ_1 η_1 ≥ 1 on all but one field, pushing symmetric MNFS up to ((36 + 16√6)/15)^{1/3} = 1.7114 (without pairwise resultants, hypothetical MNFS with η_1 = 0 would drop to c ≈ 1.4618 < 1.5263). However, this is a parametric inequality inside fixed NFS cost formulae, not an algorithmic lower bound: it misses ramified k = 1 extraction ((16/9)^{1/3} = 1.2114, [resbarrier_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/resbarrier_results.md#L248-L255)), adaptive/sparse box selection, archimedean cancellation, batch factories, and ω < 2. Importable: only the algebraic elimination of (δ_i, η_i, t, v) and the pairwise-resultant star constraint.

B. Pomerance's Size Principle (1982; ICM 1994, pp. 411–422; 2008 MSRI Publ. 44, "Smooth numbers and the quadratic sieve", §7 eq. (8) and p. 78 "A general principle, a moral, and three bullets", cited in [suffmap_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/suffmap_results.md#L228-L232)) and Random-Squares Thresholds.
- What they prove: Pomerance (2008, eq. (8)) derives the universal sampling cost L(X)^{√2+o(1)} = exp((√2 + o(1))√(ln X ln ln X)) for auxiliary integers ≤ X, whence ln X ≍ F_{2α} yields L_N[α]. For i.i.d. uniform integers in [1, X], Pomerance (ICM 1994; 1996) proved at the exponent level—and Croot–Granville–Pemantle–Tetali (Annals 2012) and Balister–Bollobás–Morris (Annals 2018) proved to exact threshold T(X) ~ e^{−γ} min_y π(y) X / Ψ(X, y)—that forming any square product requires L(X)^{√2+o(1)} draws even with NO prescribed factor base B and arbitrary large-prime combinations ([smoothbuild_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/smoothbuild_results.md#L236-L249)).
- Importable: The analyst-chosen prime cutoff B_* coupled with large-prime 2-core / chronological peeling. Importing this lets our model M_G let the algorithm use arbitrary primes, k-large-prime hypergraphs, and non-tree descent DAGs without assuming [heurnfs_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/heurnfs_results.md#L184-L190) Assumption T.

C. Other Model Lower Bounds (2000–2026).
- Generic ring / hidden-order group models: Damgård–Koprowski (2002), Sutherland (2007, Ω(N^{1/3}) order-finding), Aggarwal–Maurer (2009), Brown (2010), Jager–Schwenk (2013), Rotem–Segev (2020). Exponential lower bounds hold when integer lifts are hidden; importable only for the non-splitting diagonal-transcript principle ([leakmap_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/leakmap_results.md#L94-L120)), since smoothness inspects integer lifts.
- Index-calculus lifting and polynomial/decoder bounds: Enge–Gaudry (2002, L[1/2] framework), Silverman (SAC 2008/2009, canonical-height lower bounds blocking global-lift ECDLP index calculus), Diem (2006–2013), Coxon (2014–2021) / BGGM (2015) / Sarkar–Singh (2016) (resultant height floors), Le Gluher–Spaenlehauer–Thomé (2021, o(1) convergence), Boneh (2000/2002, Johnson-radius CRT limit, generalized in [pilist_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/pilist_results.md#L45-L55) and [sihard_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/sihard_results.md#L53-L65)), Ducas (2021) / Aboumrad–Widdows–Kaushik (2023) (Schnorr CVP refutations). None gives a compositional or adaptive L_N[1/3] relation-model theorem ([completeness_audit_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/completeness_audit_results.md#L41-L50)).


2. INDEPENDENT MODEL M_G, THEOREM G, AND PROOF SKETCH

We depart from [lowerbound_common.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/lowerbound_common.md) on three points to get a cleaner, true statement: (i) batch size K MUST be capped below N^{1/2−ε} with pre-assigned targets per query (unqualified batch amortization is false; see Adversary A1); (ii) we drop Assumption T via an analyst cutoff B_* = T^2 (ln N)^C; (iii) we prove α ≥ 1/3 and positive constants even at ω = 0 (free linear algebra).

Definitions of Model M_G (Filtered CRT-Blind Linked-Valuation Game):
- D1 [DEFINITION — State and Cost]: Input is a batch (N_1, ..., N_K) of K i.i.d. (or worst-case for K = 1) odd composite integers in [N, 2N) with 1 ≤ K ≤ N^{1/2−ε}. An algorithm is an adaptive randomized DAG with filtration (F_t)_{t=0}^T. Total cost T charges ≥ 1 per presentation registration, divisor-lattice setup, component smoothness test, and S^ω for sparse F_2 dependency extraction on S active columns (ω ∈ [0, 2]).
- D2 [MODEL-ASSUMPTION — Axiom NP (Checkable N-Publicity / CRT-Blindness)]: Each registered presentation P_m = (A_m, M_m, ψ_m, j_m) targets one N_{j_m}, with étale Q-algebra A_m = K_{m,1} × ... × K_{m,s_m} (D_m = ∑ [K_{m,ℓ} : Q] ≥ 2, D_m ≤ x^{1−δ}) and rank-r_m ≥ 2 module M_m = ⊕_{i=1}^{r_m} Z w_{m,i} ⊂ O_{A_m}, linked either by (a) unital ring maps ψ_ℓ : R_{m,ℓ} → Z/N_{j_m} agreeing on M_m (s_m ≥ 2, covering congruences, QS, NFS, MNFS, TNFS, Z-route), or (b) ramified genus/ambiguous-ideal extraction (s_m = 1). Checkable condition: evaluating ψ_m on Q-idempotents of A_m, non-resultant order indices, and generator denominators yields gcd(·, N_{j_m}) ∈ {1, N_{j_m}} (registering P_m does not split N_{j_m} at zero relations), and non-splitting external computations pass ≤ O(ln ln N) total advice bits about factors ([completeness_audit_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/completeness_audit_results.md#L165-L170)). If a side norm splits algebraically over Q into k factors, each irreducible factor is listed as its own component in A_m.
- D3 [DEFINITION — Adaptive Queries and Two-Stage Filtering]: At step t, inside a registered P_m and optional sublattice Λ_{M_t} ⊂ Z^{r_m} of known ideal modulus M_t (built from previously factored prime ideals), the algorithm picks a fresh primitive a_t ∈ Λ_{M_t} ∩ [−E_t, E_t]^{r_m} (ln E_t ≤ x^{O(1)}) and tests chosen component cofactors C_{t,ℓ} = |N_{K_{m,ℓ}}(θ(a_t)_ℓ)| / N(M_{t,ℓ}), paying ≥ 1 per tested component. Testing a shared component first and V partner components only on survivors costs 1 + V · 1_{surv} (capturing MNFS and Factory).
- D4 [HEURISTIC — Martingale Smoothness and Blind Lattice Selection (SM1, SM2, H_sel)]: Given F_{t−1}:
  (SM1) Any newly tested cofactor C_{t,ℓ} ≥ 1 is B-smooth with probability ≤ ρ(ln C_{t,ℓ} / ln B) · L_N^{o(1)}, multiplying across non-isomorphic components of a_t.
  (SM2) For any prime ℓ > B not dividing N(M_t), Pr[v_ℓ(C_t) odd | F_{t−1}] ≤ D_m (ln N)^{O(1)} / ℓ and Pr[ℓ^2 | C_t | F_{t−1}] ≤ D_m (ln N)^{O(1)} / ℓ^2.
  (H_sel, [smoothenum_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/smoothenum_results.md#L191-L197)) For Q = N(M_t) > (2 E_t)^{r_m}, E[#new primitive points in Λ_{M_t} ∩ [−E_t, E_t]^{r_m} | F_{t−1}] ≤ O((2 E_t)^{r_m} / Q), and non-cusp sublevel counts on Λ_{M_t} scale by Q^{−(D_m−r_m)/D_m}.
- D5 [PROVED at r = 2 and GP small-box r ≥ 3; MODEL-ASSUMPTION LP_exc^rel otherwise — Arithmetic Sublevel Floor]: For non-coincident P_m with N_j^{k_m} | Δ(P_m), the count N_ind(P_m, E; X) of unit-inequivalent, proper-subspace-independent primitive points in [−E, E]^{r_m} with 0 < |W_m(a)| ≤ X satisfies ≤ O(D_m N_j^{−k_m (r_m−1)/(D_m(D_m−1))} X^{r_m/D_m}) + O(D_m (ln E + 1)) (proved unconditionally for r_m = 2 by Bean + Lemma FT in [subthird_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/subthird_results.md#L55-L62), and up to boundary error (2E)^{r−1} for GP/framed r_m ≥ 3 by [rank3_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/rank3_results.md#L126-L195) and [rankdegen_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/rankdegen_results.md#L99-L103); assumed as LP_exc^rel for degenerate/large-box r_m ≥ 3 alongside proved generator floor Theorem KH, [subthird_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/subthird_results.md#L27-L40)).
- D6 [HEURISTIC — Axiom R (Per-Field Rank Floor)]: Extracting a factor of N_j requires a non-empty F_2-dependency D_j of relations for N_j (covering F_2 square roots and Z-route integer kernels via Lemma XK-Z, [zroute_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/zroute_results.md#L135-L155)). If D_j uses only prime ideals of norm ≤ B_v in an active non-isomorphic field K_v, then K_v contributes R_v ≥ B_v^{1−o(1)} relations to D_j; if V_+ active fields link through a shared component K_0 at bound B_0, ∑_{v=1}^{V_+} R_v ≥ B_0^{1−o(1)}.

Theorem G [MODEL-PROVED in M_G]:
1. (Universal All-N Floor, ω = 0, No Assumption T): Every algorithm in M_G factoring any odd composite N with probability ≥ 1/2 costs T ≥ L_N[1/3, c_0]. Specifically: if D_1 uses any prime ideal above B_* := T^2 (ln N)^C (arbitrary descent DAGs / large-prime hypergraphs), T ≥ L_N[1/3, (k/18)^{1/3}] (0.3816 for k = 1, 0.4807 for k = 2); if supported below B_*, T ≥ L_N[1/3, (16k/9)^{1/3}] — giving 1.2114 (k = 1 ramified) and (32/9)^{1/3} = 1.5263 (k = 2 ring-map, tight for SNFS), even with free linear algebra (ω = 0).
2. (Almost-All-N Tight MNFS Bound): Under full-box/typical-norm profile on P_m, for 1 − o(1) of N ∈ [N_0, 2N_0), T ≥ L_N[1/3, c_M] with c_M = ((92 + 26√13)/27)^{1/3} = 1.9019 at ω = 2 (tight for MNFS), and T ≥ L_N[1/3, 1.8595] at ω = 0.
3. (Amortized Factory Bound): For 1 ≤ K ≤ N^{1/2−ε} i.i.d. semiprimes in [N_0, 2N_0) under the same profile, total cost satisfies T ≥ max(L_N[1/3, c_M], K · L_N[1/3, c_fact]) with c_fact = 2((2 + √6)/6)^{2/3} = 1.6386 at ω = 2 (tight for Coppersmith's factory) and 1.6363 at ω = 0.

Proof Sketch (with exact status and gaps):
- Step 1 (Advice, Linking, and Batch Decoupling — [PROVED]): Enumerating O(ln ln N) external advice bits multiplies T by poly(ln N) = L_N^{o(1)} ([completeness_audit_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/completeness_audit_results.md#L165-L170)). By [resbarrier_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/resbarrier_results.md#L133-L172) Lemma ND and [rankdegen_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/rankdegen_results.md#L190-L199) Lemma CC, Axiom NP implies that any presentation contributing non-trivially to D_j is non-coincident and satisfies N_j^{k_m} | Δ(P_m) (k_m = 2 for two-component ring-map, k_m = 1 for ramified). For K ≤ N^{1/2−ε} i.i.d. targets and T ≤ N^{o(1)} per target, a candidate computed for N_{j_1} (or during precomputation) satisfies a linking divisibility for another N_{j_2} with probability ≤ τ(Res) K / N_0^{1−o(1)} = o(1), so accepted relations partition cleanly across j = 1, ..., K; only N-independent tables (like rational-smooth pairs a − bm) amortize across j.
- Step 2 (Chronological Last-Hit Elimination of Assumption T — [MODEL-PROVED]): Set B_* = T^2 (ln N)^C with ln T = c F_α. Let L_+(D_j) be the prime ideals of norm > B_* occurring to odd power in D_j. Suppose L_+ ≠ ∅. Every q ∈ L_+ appears oddly in ≥ 2 distinct steps of D_j (Lemma KI, [smoothbuild_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/smoothbuild_results.md#L186-L195)); let t_max(q) be its last chronological step in D_j, and set t_last := max_{q ∈ L_+} t_max(q). Across all pairs 1 ≤ t_1 < t_2 ≤ T, SM2 bounds expected unforced repeats above B_* (and unforced squares > B_*^2) by O(T^2 D (ln N)^{O(1)} / B_*) = o(1). Thus w.h.p. every q ∈ L_+ dividing W(a_{t_last}) MUST divide the forced modulus M_{t_last}, while no prime > B_* divides the unforced cofactor C_{t_last} = |W(a_{t_last})| / N(M_{t_last})—meaning t_last has Q = N(M_{t_last}) > B_* and a 100% B_*-smooth cofactor! At r = 2, G = (W ∘ M)/Q has |disc G| = |disc W| Q^{(D−1)(D−2)} ≥ N^k Q^{(D−1)(D−2)} ([resbarrier_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/resbarrier_results.md#L205-L210)); Bean + Lemma FT + H_sel force ln C_{t_last} ≥ kx/(2(D−1)) + ((D−2)/2) ln B_* ≥ √(kx ln B_*). Testing for B_*-smoothness in ≤ T steps via SM1 requires F_α ≥ Ω(F_{(1−α)/2}), forcing α ≥ 1/3 and, at α = 1/3 (ln B_* = 2c F_{1/3}), c ≥ (1/3)√(k/(2c)), i.e. c ≥ (k/18)^{1/3}. [GAP G1: At degenerate/large-box rank r ≥ 3, this sublattice floor invokes LP_exc^rel.]
- Step 3 (Multi-Family and Star Composition below B_* — [MODEL-PROVED]): Now assume L_+(D_j) = ∅ (all active primes ≤ B_*). Group D_j's relations by non-isomorphic field components K_v. Because distinct fields have disjoint prime-ideal columns, each active K_v has an effective smoothness max B_v ≤ B_* and, by Axiom R, requires R_v ≥ B_v^{1−o(1)} relations. Partitioning examined candidates in each presentation into O(ln x) dyadic norm buckets (1+ε)^s, D5 bounds the count in bucket X by N_j^{−k(r−1)/(D(D−1))} X^{r/D} (for R_v ≫ D ln E).
  (a) Disjoint families: If M_0 families share no component, total cost is ∑_{m=1}^{M_0} T_m where each active family m independently achieves R_m ≥ B_m^{1−o(1)}, so T ≥ min_m T_m (convexity kills disjoint mixing!). Optimizing r ≥ 2 gives κ_r = (r−1)/(D−1), minimized at r = 2 ([rank3_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/rank3_results.md#L68-L71)). At r = 2, even with ω = 0, R ≥ B forces 2e − 2√(κ e)/(3b) ≥ b (κ = k/2); since max_b 3b(2e − b) = 3e^2 (at b = e), 3e^2 ≥ 2√(κ e), proving 2e ≥ (16k/9)^{1/3}.
  (b) Star/MNFS composition: If V_+ = L_N[1/3, v] active fields f_1, ..., f_{V_+} share a base component g (smoothness bound B_0), pairwise resultant divisibility N_j | Res(f_u, f_w) forces 2 δ_1 η_1 ≥ 1 on all but one f_u, so without GAE the star floor stays ≥ (32/9)^{1/3}. For 1 − o(1) of N_j, Theorem GAE ([resbarrier_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/resbarrier_results.md#L267-L292)) forces base-m heights η_0, η_1 ≥ 1/δ. Enforcing N_0 = L[2e], survivors S_0 ≤ N_0 L[−1/(3 b_0 δ)], partner tests ∑ N_v = L[2e − 1/(3 b_0 δ) + v], ∑ R_v ≥ s = max(b_0, b_v + v), and LA L[ω s] yields exact minimum c_M = 1.9019 at ω = 2 and 1.8595 at ω = 0. Setting shared precomputation N_0 free per target (for K ≤ N^{1/2−ε}) while retaining per-target partner tests S_0 and R_j ≥ max(b_0, b_v) yields c_fact = 1.6386 at ω = 2 (1.6363 at ω = 0). [GAP G2: Axiom R is heuristic beyond uniform integers. GAP G3: GAE bounds polynomial heights, needing full-box/typical-norm dominance to prevent SL_2(R)-skewed thin sub-boxes from dropping to the SNFS floor 1.5263.]

Inclusion Table (Known Algorithms Inside M_G):
- Dixon / CFRAC / QS / MPQS: Inside (D = 2, k = 1 or congruence floor x/2) → reproduces L_N[1/2, 1] tight.
- GNFS (2-poly, base-m or Kleinjung/Montgomery, any d_1 + d_2): Inside → reproduces L_N[1/3, (64/9)^{1/3} = 1.9230] tight.
- MNFS (Coppersmith 1-rational + V-algebraic star): Inside via D3 two-stage filtering → reproduces L_N[1/3, 1.9019] tight.
- SNFS and Kirchner ramified class-group NFS: Inside → reproduces (32/9)^{1/3} = 1.5263 (k = 2) and (16/9)^{1/3} = 1.2114 (k = 1) tight.
- TNFS-like towers, t-dim sieving (t ≥ 3), rank-r linked modules: Inside (under LP_exc^rel at degenerate/large-box r ≥ 3) → η cancels or worsens ([heurnfs_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/heurnfs_results.md#L353-L377)); t = r = 2 optimal.
- Line / special-q lattice sieving, batch ECM, k-large-prime variants, multi-level descent DAGs: Inside (Step 2 + Prop LQ) → L^{o(1)} gain; α ≥ 1/3 without Assumption T.
- Factorization factory / Batch NFS (for K ≤ N^{1/2−ε}): Inside → reproduces 1.6386 RAM per N tight.
- Adaptive candidate selectors and leak→relation hybrids (≤ O(ln ln N) bits), plus Z-route ([zroute_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/zroute_results.md#L135-L155)): Inside → α ≥ 1/3.


3. ADVERSARY: NATURAL ALGORITHMS VIOLATING THE ASSUMPTIONS, EXCLUSIONS, AND WEAKEST POINTS

A1. Dense-Batch Doubly-Smooth Difference Factory (violates unqualified batch desideratum in [lowerbound_common.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/lowerbound_common.md#L16-L17) and M_G's K ≤ N^{1/2−ε} / pre-assigned target rule):
- Construction: Given K distinct semiprimes N_1, ..., N_K ∈ [N, 2N) in a hash set, fix B = (ln N)^3. Enumerate bottom-up B-smooth sets U_0 ⊂ [2N, 5N/2] of size 8 N^{1/2} (ln N)^4 and V_0 ⊂ [N/2, N] of size 8 N^{1/2} (valid unconditionally since Ψ(N, (ln N)^3) = N^{2/3−o(1)} ≫ N^{1/2}). For each (u, v) ∈ U_0 × V_0, if m := u − v lies in {N_1, ..., N_K}, record u ≡ v (mod m)—a certified doubly-(ln N)^3-smooth relation with zero gcd splits or trial division! Solve each target's (ln N)^3 × (ln N)^3 F_2 matrix. Total work is O(N (ln N)^4 + K (ln N)^9): for K = Θ(N ln ln N / ln N), amortized cost is (ln N)^{O(1)} per semiprime (α = 0 < 1/3)! (With gcd splits allowed, Bernstein remainder-tree trial division already gives poly(ln N) per target at K = N^{1/2}.)
- Verdict: Shows the preamble's unqualified batch desideratum is TOO STRONG (literally false!). M_G's cap K ≤ N^{1/2−ε} is essential and natural.

A2. Beyond-Johnson Class-Group 2D-CRT List Decoder (M2 in [subthird_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/subthird_results.md#L76-L79); violates H_sel / SM1):
- Construction: Set β = 1/4, B = L_N[1/4, κ], box [1, K_0]^2 with K_0 = L_N[3/4, ν]. Sample π(B) random known-exponent ideals in Cl(−4N) with reduced norm forms Q_m(k, v) ≈ √N, compute their O(B) public residues mod q^{e_q} (q ≤ B)—which information-theoretically pin every B-smooth witness ([sinonobliv_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/sinonobliv_results.md#L60-L64))—and apply an algebraic list-decoder above counting capacity (agreement/entropy ≍ (x/ln x)^{1/4} → ∞, below Johnson √(kn)) to output one smooth (k, v) in B^{O(1)} time, factoring N in L_N[1/4].
- Verdict: Shows the model is TOO STRONG (a genuine model fudge, NOT factoring in disguise). Inputs are 100% N-public, positive-definite Δ = −4N < 0 resists known F_p-DL reductions ([equivtarget_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/equivtarget_results.md#L50)), and H_sel excludes sub-Johnson CRT decoding by fiat because we lack superpolynomial arithmetic circuit lower bounds ([crtdecode_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/crtdecode_results.md#L67-L71)).

A3. Multi-Cone Unit-Cancelled Type-D Module (LP_exc^rel in [subthird_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/subthird_results.md#L83-L95); violates D5 at degenerate r ≥ 3):
- Construction: Over k = Q(ζ_7)^+ (e = 3, unit rank 2) splitting mod N, build a relative-rank-m ≥ 3 linked O_k-module (d = en ≍ √x, r = em ≍ x^{1/4}). Despite Theorem KH forcing generator height H ≳ x^{3/4}, apply LLL across L_N[1/4] incomparable unit-weighted cones (V_F = ∞ under O_k^×) to find sparse vectors whose archimedean cancellations drop |W(a)| to exp(O(√(x ln x))), giving L_N[1/4].
- Verdict: Shows D5 is PARTIALLY TOO STRONG (an unproved Diophantine counting assumption at r ≥ 3, though empirically supported: 0 incremental rank in [subthird_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/subthird_results.md#L50-L54) and [equivtarget_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/equivtarget_results.md#L55)).

A4. Growing-k Correlated-Smoothness / Shifted-Product Families (violates naive 1-integer SM1; [suffmap_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/suffmap_results.md#L153-L155), [pilist_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/pilist_results.md#L68-L75)):
- Construction: Use Aurifeuillian/Galois identities or non-exact PTE pencils P_A(m) − P_B(m) = kN + v where P_A(x) = ∏_{i=1}^k (x − a_i) splits into k → ∞ linear factors over Z, boosting smoothness from ρ(u) to ρ(u/k)^k ≈ k^u ρ(u) (up to 1 when k = u).
- Verdict: For k = O(1), k^u = L_N^{o(1)} stays inside M_G. For k → ∞, M_G splits P_A into k separate Q-components (where pairwise Res kills the height gain) unless pre-multiplied bottom-up as a smooth constructor (see A5). Excluding bottom-up constructors is a model restriction (fudge for single-interval constants, borderline DL-disguise for sub-1/3).

A5. Adaptive Residue-Steered Interval / Bohr Constructor (Prop SI in [suffmap_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/suffmap_results.md#L318-L366), [sihard_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/sihard_results.md#L66-L75)):
- Construction: Adaptively steer prime products into I_k = [kN, kN + L_N[2/3, ν]] using modular residuals to get y-smooth u_k in L_N^{o(1)} time and test v_k = u_k − kN, achieving L_N[1/3, 1.2114]; or steer into a Bohr set |u mod N| ≤ L_N[2α] for L_N[α < 1/3].
- Verdict: Single-interval Prop SI proves any c_M > 1.2114 bound is TOO STRONG for constructive methods, while confirming α ≥ 1/3 holds (max(α, 1 − 2α) ≥ 1/3). The sub-1/3 Bohr constructor reduces F_p-DL to L_p[α] (Prop DLT) and unbounded coset navigation is FACT ∧ DL ([navigate_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/navigate_results.md#L45-L50)), so excluding Bohr navigation as DL/factoring-in-disguise is natural, provided it is flagged explicitly.

A6. Retained PRIM / Compressed-Factorial Pre-Stage ([leakmap_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/leakmap_results.md#L69-L76), [multcopp_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/multcopp_results.md#L67-L73); violates Axiom NP):
- Construction: Run nested gates x_{i+1} = (x_i^N + c_i)^N mod N or short Pochhammer SLPs for ⌊√N⌋! mod N to extract n/4 bits of p (or split N directly) before Coppersmith/NFS.
- Verdict: EXCLUDE (natural). These are non-relational direct-splitting or τ-conjecture-violating algebraic-circuit attacks ([suffmap_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/suffmap_results.md#L486-L514)), outside the relation paradigm.

Exclusion Summary (Natural vs Fudge):
- Axiom NP (idempotent blindness, ≤ O(ln ln N) non-split external bits) and K ≤ N^{1/2−ε}: NATURAL (excludes pre-split algebras, non-relational circuits, and cross-target dense routing).
- SM1/H_sel (excluding sub-Johnson CRT decoders M2 and Prop SI constructors): FUDGE (substitutes an oracle access rule for an unproved computational hardness theorem on public residues).
- LP_exc^rel (degenerate/large-box rank r ≥ 3) and Axiom R (sub-B_v subspace independence): PARTIAL FUDGE (plausible arithmetic/combinatorial conjectures, proved only in r = 2 / GP / uniform-integer cases).

The 3 Weakest Points of the Argument:
1. H_sel / SM1 vs Public-Syndrome Decoders (Adversary A2): Because O(B) residues mod q^{e_q} information-theoretically determine all smooth points in a box, pricing smoothness via point/sublattice queries rather than arbitrary circuits on the residue table assumes away beyond-Johnson 2D quadratic CRT list decoding.
2. Unproved Sublevel Counting in Unit-Infinite Higher Rank (LP_exc^rel, Adversary A3): At rank r ≥ 3 with Δ_F = 0 (type-D subfield modules where O_k^× acts) or huge boxes E > B^{1/(r−1)}, Theorem KH bounds generator heights, not cancelled linear combinations; closing the gap to α = 1/4 rests on an open Diophantine counting hypothesis.
3. Axiom R and the Height-to-Area Gap (Gaps G2–G3): Unlike CGPT/BBM for uniform integers, no theorem rules out polynomial families generating O(poly(ln N))-row F_2-dependencies over small primes, and Theorem GAE bounds polynomial heights rather than SL_2(R)-invariant sublevel areas on sparse adaptive sub-boxes (leaving worst-case c_0 = 1.2114 / 1.5263 below MNFS 1.9019 without a full-box profile).
